      "text": "Motivic periods and P^1 minus 3 points — This is a review of the theory of the motivic fundamental group of the projective line minus three points, and its relation to multiple zeta values.\n\n**Motivic periods and P^1 minus 3 points**\n\n*Francis Brown∗*\n\n25 pp, 9 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** This is a review of the theory of the motivic fundamental group of the projective line minus three points, and its relation to multiple zeta values. Mathematics Subject Classiﬁcation (2010). Primary 11M32; Secondary 14C15.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 3 The main theorem and consequences; 3.2 Transcendence conjectures.; 4 Roots of unity; 5 Depth; 6 Multiple modular values; 1 −→UΓ −→GΓ −→S −→1; 7 References",
